    "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>ABOUT THIS GAME</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>SHOPSKA SALAD\u00a0</strong>is a <strong>first-person folklore horror</strong> set in rural Bulgaria, where <strong>slow-burn dread</strong>, <strong>psychological unease</strong>, and <strong>ritualistic gameplay</strong> intertwine.<br>You're just here to tidy up your late \u0431\u0430\u0431\u0430\u2019s (grandmother\u2019s) cottage before it\u2019s sold\u2026<br>But the quiet routines she followed begin to <strong>stir something ancient</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Forget the ritual\u2026 and the house forgets you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>FEATURES</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>No Cheap Scares</strong><br>Horror that creeps instead of jumps. Fear grows from silence, memory, and the uncanny.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong> Folklore</strong><br>Explore traditions like the <strong>Surva Festival</strong>, <strong>Kukeri spirits</strong>, and sacred home rituals - presented with <strong>cultural respect</strong> and <strong>symbolic weight</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Immersive Mundanity</strong><br>Cook, clean, light the fire, tend to icons. Simple routines slowly unravel into something terrifying.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Dynamic Ritual System</strong><br>Your actions matter. <strong>Five different endings</strong> await, shaped by what you choose to honor - or ignore.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Retro Realism</strong><br>Aesthetic inspired by <strong>PS1-era horror</strong>, VHS filters, and analog dread.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>You Are Not Alone</strong><br>They see what you do. They see what you don\u2019t.\u00a0\ud83e\uddcd </p>",
    "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>ABOUT THIS GAME</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>SHOPSKA SALAD\u00a0</strong>is a <strong>first-person folklore horror</strong> set in rural Bulgaria, where <strong>slow-burn dread</strong>, <strong>psychological unease</strong>, and <strong>ritualistic gameplay</strong> intertwine.<br>You're just here to tidy up your late \u0431\u0430\u0431\u0430\u2019s (grandmother\u2019s) cottage before it\u2019s sold\u2026<br>But the quiet routines she followed begin to <strong>stir something ancient</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Forget the ritual\u2026 and the house forgets you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>FEATURES</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>No Cheap Scares</strong><br>Horror that creeps instead of jumps. Fear grows from silence, memory, and the uncanny.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong> Folklore</strong><br>Explore traditions like the <strong>Surva Festival</strong>, <strong>Kukeri spirits</strong>, and sacred home rituals - presented with <strong>cultural respect</strong> and <strong>symbolic weight</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Immersive Mundanity</strong><br>Cook, clean, light the fire, tend to icons. Simple routines slowly unravel into something terrifying.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Dynamic Ritual System</strong><br>Your actions matter. <strong>Five different endings</strong> await, shaped by what you choose to honor - or ignore.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Retro Realism</strong><br>Aesthetic inspired by <strong>PS1-era horror</strong>, VHS filters, and analog dread.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>You Are Not Alone</strong><br>They see what you do. They see what you don\u2019t.\u00a0\ud83e\uddcd </p>",
